window.ORBIT_DOC_PAGES = {"index.html": {"title": "Orbit — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"orbit\">Orbit</h1>\n<div class=\"hero\">\n<img src=\"../logos/orbit.png\" alt=\"Orbit logo\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"kicker\">Documentation · Orbit for Windows</p>\n<p class=\"name\">All your creative tools, in one app</p>\n<p class=\"tag\">Download, convert, enhance and create: video, audio, image and 3D, with AI tools that run on\nyour own computer.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"badges\">\n<span>Windows 10 and 11</span>\n<span>24 tools</span>\n<span>Local AI (GPU)</span>\n<span>English, Français, Español, Deutsch, Italiano, Português</span>\n</div>\n\n<h2 id=\"what-orbit-does\">What Orbit does</h2>\n<p>Orbit brings into one window tools you would usually find in a dozen programs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>download</strong> videos, playlists and music from hundreds of sites (YouTube, TikTok, Twitch, Spotify, Deezer,\n  file hosts…) and follow your favourite channels;</li>\n<li><strong>convert</strong> almost any file: video (accelerated by NVIDIA graphics cards), audio, image, LUT, fonts, 3D\n  models, documents, After Effects presets;</li>\n<li><strong>enhance and create with AI</strong>: generate images, erase or replace an object, remove a background, upscale a\n  video, make it smoother, turn an image into a 3D model, a photo into a PBR material, a video into a 3D animation (mocap), retouch a video shot;</li>\n<li><strong>work on sound</strong>: split vocals from music, denoise, normalize, transcribe and subtitle;</li>\n<li><strong>create sound with AI</strong>: voice-overs and voice cloning, dubbing a video into another language, sound\n  effects, music, live voice changer;</li>\n<li><strong>organize and share</strong>: media library, a toolbox of more than 60 small tools, encrypted cloud storage, folder sync and sharing with others.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Most AI tools run <strong>on your computer</strong>: your files never leave your machine, and once the models are\ndownloaded, they work offline.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/home.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Orbit home screen: every tool, sorted by category\" src=\"images/home.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Orbit home screen: every tool, sorted by category</figcaption></figure>\n<p class=\"gallery g3\"><img src=\"../showcase/cite-flottante.jpg\" alt=\"Made with AI Generation: a floating city\"><img src=\"../showcase/robot-cafe.jpg\" alt=\"Made with AI Generation: a robot in a retro café\"><img src=\"../showcase/montagne.jpg\" alt=\"Made with AI Generation: a mountain as a vector illustration\"></p>\n\n<h2 id=\"contents\">Contents</h2>\n<div class=\"cards\">\n<a href=\"installation.html\">Installation<small>Install Orbit, first launch, updates.</small></a>\n<a href=\"interface.html\">The interface<small>Home, search, menu, AI assistant.</small></a>\n<a href=\"telechargements.html\">Downloads<small>Videos, music, playlists, subscriptions.</small></a>\n<a href=\"conversion.html\">Conversion<small>Universal converter and HandBrake.</small></a>\n<a href=\"ia-image.html\">AI for images<small>Generation, magic eraser, cutout, enhance.</small></a>\n<a href=\"ia-video-3d.html\">AI for video and 3D<small>Interpolation, Topaz, Paint a plate, 3D, PBR, mocap.</small></a>\n<a href=\"voix-musique-ia.html\">Voice, dubbing and music AI<small>Voice-over, dubbing, foley, music, voice changer.</small></a>\n<a href=\"audio-transcription.html\">Audio and transcription<small>Audio Studio, automatic subtitles.</small></a>\n<a href=\"boite-a-outils.html\">Toolbox and media library<small>More than 60 quick tools, your media.</small></a>\n<a href=\"drive.html\">Orbit Drive<small>Encrypted storage, folder sync, sharing.</small></a>\n<a href=\"reglages.html\">Settings<small>Every settings page, graphics card.</small></a>\n<a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium<small>What is included and how to activate it.</small></a>\n<a href=\"depannage.html\">Troubleshooting<small>Common problems and their fixes.</small></a>\n</div>\n\n<h2 id=\"what-you-need\">What you need</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Minimum</th>\n<th>For the AI tools</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>System</td>\n<td>Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit</td>\n<td>Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Memory</td>\n<td>8 GB</td>\n<td>16 GB or more</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Graphics card</td>\n<td>Any recent card</td>\n<td>NVIDIA RTX, 8 GB of video memory or more (16 GB for 3D and Paint a plate)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Disk</td>\n<td>1 GB for the app</td>\n<td>From a few GB to more than 60 GB depending on the AI models installed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Internet</td>\n<td>To download, and for the first install of the models</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Download, conversion and toolbox features work on any PC. The AI tools use the graphics card when there is one;\nsome (AI 3D Creation, Paint a plate, local AI Generation, AI Voice, Dubbing, Foley, Music, PBR Materials, Mocap)\nneed an <strong>NVIDIA</strong> card.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"next\" href=\"installation.html\"><span>Next</span>Installation</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#what-orbit-does\">What Orbit does</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#contents\">Contents</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#what-you-need\">What you need</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../index.html"}, "installation.html": {"title": "Installation — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"installation\">Installation</h1>\n<h2 id=\"install-orbit\">Install Orbit</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Download the installer: the <strong>Download Orbit</strong> button at the top left of this page, or the\n   <a href=\"https://github.com/ThomasDM40-dev/orbit-releases/releases/latest\">Orbit releases page</a> (file\n   <code>Orbit-Installer.exe</code>).</li>\n<li>Run <code>Orbit-Installer.exe</code> and follow the install window.</li>\n<li>At the end, click the launch button: Orbit opens.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Orbit installs for your Windows account only (no administrator rights needed) and creates an <strong>Orbit</strong>\nshortcut on the desktop and in the Start menu.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If Windows shows \"Windows protected your PC\", click <strong>More info</strong> then <strong>Run anyway</strong>. This message appears for\nrecent apps that Windows does not know yet.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"first-launch\">First launch</h2>\n<p>On first launch, Orbit asks what you do (video editor, motion design, 3D, audio, downloading, image\ncreation…). It then shows only the tools you need; <strong>I want to explore everything</strong> keeps them all. At the\nbottom, you also pick the theme and the accent color.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/onboarding.jpg\"><img alt=\"The setup wizard: pick what you do, Orbit arranges its tools\" src=\"images/onboarding.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The setup wizard: pick what you do, Orbit arranges its tools</figcaption></figure>\n<p>You can run this wizard again at any time: <strong>Settings › Appearance › Setup wizard › Relaunch</strong>. Hidden tabs stay\nreachable through search (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd>) and the <strong>Menu</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"modules-installed-on-demand\">Modules installed on demand</h2>\n<p>Orbit stays light: heavy engines are only downloaded the first time you need them (ffmpeg, yt-dlp, AI engines,\nmodels). Each tool shows an <strong>Install</strong> button when something is missing, with a progress bar. The <strong>Settings ›\nModules &amp; AI</strong> page lists every module, its size and its state, and installs or updates them in one go.</p>\n<p>Modules and models live in the <code>.orbit</code> folder of your user folder (<code>C:\\Users\\&lt;you&gt;\\.orbit</code>). <strong>Settings ›\nSystem › Orbit data folder › Open</strong> shows it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"updates\">Updates</h2>\n<p>Orbit updates itself: at launch, it checks for a new version, downloads it in the background and installs it\nat the next restart. After an update, a window presents what is new.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>To check by hand: <strong>Settings › About › Check for updates</strong>.</li>\n<li>The download engine (yt-dlp) also updates itself at every launch, to keep up with site changes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If a version is too old, the AI tools show <strong>Update required</strong> with a button that installs the latest version.</p>\n<h2 id=\"uninstall\">Uninstall</h2>\n<p><strong>Windows Settings › Apps › Installed apps</strong>, find <strong>Orbit</strong>, then <strong>Uninstall</strong>. The <code>.orbit</code> folder\n(modules, AI models, settings) is not removed: delete it by hand to get the disk space back.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"index.html\"><span>Previous</span>Orbit</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"interface.html\"><span>Next</span>The interface</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#install-orbit\">Install Orbit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#first-launch\">First launch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#modules-installed-on-demand\">Modules installed on demand</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#updates\">Updates</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#uninstall\">Uninstall</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../installation.html"}, "interface.html": {"title": "The interface — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"the-interface\">The interface</h1>\n<h2 id=\"home\">Home</h2>\n<p>The home screen shows every tool, sorted into five categories: <strong>Download</strong>, <strong>Conversion</strong>, <strong>Creative AI</strong>,\n<strong>Studio &amp; Tools</strong> and <strong>Cloud</strong>. The <strong>Trending</strong> and <strong>New</strong> rows highlight the most used and the latest\ntools. Click a card to open the tool.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/home.jpg\"><img alt=\"The home screen\" src=\"images/home.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The home screen</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The <strong>sidebar</strong> on the left stays visible everywhere: it lists the tools by category, with <strong>Premium</strong> (your\nlicence state) and <strong>Settings</strong> at the bottom. In a small window it folds away: the menu button at the top left\nopens it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"search-ctrlk\">Search (Ctrl+K)</h2>\n<p>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> anywhere, or click the search box at the top: type a few letters, then\n<kbd>Enter</kbd> to open the tool. Search also finds the tools you have hidden.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/search.jpg\"><img alt=\"Quick search\" src=\"images/search.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Quick search</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"the-menu\">The Menu</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Menu</strong> button, at the top right, groups the general commands:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>File</strong>: Premium, Settings, <strong>Import</strong> (a list of links), open the download folder, Quit;</li>\n<li><strong>Downloads</strong>: pause all, resume all, restart failed downloads, clear finished ones, cancel all;</li>\n<li><strong>Language</strong>: English, French, Spanish, German, Italian, Portuguese;</li>\n<li><strong>Tools</strong>: open the Orbit folder, reinstall or update yt-dlp, changelog, back up and restore subscriptions,\n  AI Assistant;</li>\n<li>tab visibility: tick or untick the tools to show in the sidebar.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure><a href=\"images/menu.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Menu\" src=\"images/menu.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Menu</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Next to it, the speaker icon mutes or restores the small interface sounds.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-ai-assistant\">The AI assistant</h2>\n<p>The round button at the bottom right opens <strong>Orbit AI</strong>, an assistant that knows the app. Ask it what you want\nto do (\"compress this video for Discord\", \"where do I set the quality?\"): it answers, opens the right tool or\nchanges a setting for you. You can also drop a file on it.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/assistant.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Orbit AI assistant\" src=\"images/assistant.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Orbit AI assistant</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The assistant uses a free local AI (about 2 GB, downloaded once, works offline) or, if you add your own key,\nAnthropic's Claude: <strong>Settings › AI &amp; Performance › AI Assistant</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"task-center\">Task center</h2>\n<p>Long jobs (conversions, AI renders, encodes) show up in the <strong>task center</strong> with their progress, even when you\nswitch tabs. AI tools that use the graphics card run one at a time: a waiting job shows <strong>Waiting for a GPU\nslot…</strong> (set in <strong>Settings › Downloads › Simultaneous AI jobs (GPU)</strong>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"drag-and-drop\">Drag and drop</h2>\n<p>Almost every tool accepts files dragged from Windows Explorer, one at a time or many at once. You can also add\n<strong>Orbit</strong> to Explorer's right-click menu (<strong>Settings › Downloads › Windows right-click menu</strong>) to compress or\ncrop a file without opening the app.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"installation.html\"><span>Previous</span>Installation</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"telechargements.html\"><span>Next</span>Downloads</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#home\">Home</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#search-ctrlk\">Search (Ctrl+K)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-menu\">The Menu</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-ai-assistant\">The AI assistant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#task-center\">Task center</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#drag-and-drop\">Drag and drop</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../interface.html"}, "telechargements.html": {"title": "Downloads — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"downloads\">Downloads</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Only download content you have the right to copy: your own videos, royalty-free content, or for a use allowed\nby the law of your country.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"download-a-video\">Download a video</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Copy the link of the video (YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, X, Vimeo, Twitch, SoundCloud… several hundred sites\n   are supported).</li>\n<li>In the <strong>Downloads</strong> tab, paste it in the top bar (clipboard button on the left, or\n   <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd>). Orbit analyzes the link and shows the title and thumbnail.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Download</strong> to start right away, or press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to <strong>queue</strong> it and start everything later\n   with <strong>Download all</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure><a href=\"images/downloads.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Downloads tab with finished, queued and failed items\" src=\"images/downloads.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Downloads tab with finished, queued and failed items</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Files go to the folder shown at the top right (<strong>Downloads</strong> by default); click it to change it. Each item can\nalso have its own folder (folder icon on its row).</p>\n<h2 id=\"quality-and-format\">Quality and format</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Highest Quality</strong> button, on the right of the bar, opens the format choice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Download Audio Only?</strong>: a switch to keep only the sound (MP3, FLAC, WAV, M4A, OGG);</li>\n<li><strong>Download Format</strong>: from <strong>Highest Quality Video and Audio</strong> to 8K, 4K, 2K, 1080p, 720p, 480p, 360p, 144p, or\n  standard MP4;</li>\n<li><strong>Thumbnail</strong>: <strong>Off</strong>, <strong>Separate image</strong>, <strong>Embedded in the video</strong> or <strong>Both</strong>, with the image format (JPG,\n  PNG, WEBP) and size.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This choice applies to the next links. For a queued item, the drop-down list on its row changes its own format.</p>\n<p>The icons of the bar turn on options for the next links:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Icon</th>\n<th>Effect</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SNIFFER</strong></td>\n<td>opens the built-in browser to catch hidden videos on a page (see below)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Document</td>\n<td>imports a playlist exported as CSV (Exportify, TuneMyMusic, Soundiiz)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Image</td>\n<td>thumbnail (set in the quality menu)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>List</td>\n<td>downloads the whole playlist instead of one video</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CC</td>\n<td>embeds subtitles in the file</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cookie</td>\n<td>uses your browser's cookies (Chrome) for content that needs a login</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Permanent settings (H.264 forced for editing, metadata, chapters, SponsorBlock, automatic subtitles…) are in\n<strong>Settings › Downloads</strong>, see <a href=\"reglages.html#downloads\">Settings</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-download-list\">The download list</h2>\n<p>Each row shows the source, the state, then the resolution, codecs, duration, size and container once the file\nis ready. The buttons on the right depend on the state:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Queued</strong>: pick the format, the folder, <strong>Download</strong>, or <strong>…</strong> for <strong>Advanced options (Trimmer /\n  Scheduler)</strong>:<ul>\n<li><strong>Trimmer</strong>: keep only a part (start and end, for example <code>01:20</code> and <code>02:45</code>);</li>\n<li><strong>Scheduler</strong>: start the download at a set time.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Active</strong>: pause, resume, cancel; the row shows the speed and the time left.</li>\n<li><strong>Done</strong>: <strong>Play in Orbit</strong> (built-in player), open the folder, remove from the list.</li>\n<li><strong>File deleted</strong>: the file is no longer on disk; <strong>Download again</strong> gets it back.</li>\n<li><strong>Failed — see logs</strong>: the log explains the error; <strong>Retry</strong> starts again.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At the top of the list: the counters (<strong>Queued</strong>, <strong>Done</strong>, <strong>Failed</strong>), sorting (<strong>Date</strong>, <strong>Name</strong>,\n<strong>Size</strong>), three views (grid, list, compact) and <strong>Clear</strong> to remove finished items.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If Orbit or Windows closes during a download, Orbit resumes it at the next launch where it stopped.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"music-spotify-apple-music-deezer-and-csv\">Music: Spotify, Apple Music, Deezer and CSV</h2>\n<p>Paste a <strong>Spotify</strong> link (track, album, playlist or artist), an <strong>Apple Music</strong> link or a <strong>Deezer</strong> link in the same bar. Orbit reads\nthe track list, finds each song on YouTube Music and saves it with its title, artist, album and cover (and\nsynced <code>.lrc</code> lyrics when they exist).</p>\n<p>Spotify only shows the first 100 tracks of a playlist. For a longer playlist, export it as CSV (with Exportify,\nTuneMyMusic or Soundiiz) then import the file with the <strong>Document</strong> icon of the bar.</p>\n<p>Orbit bypasses no protection: the sound comes from the public versions found on YouTube Music, not from\nSpotify.</p>\n<h2 id=\"twitch\">Twitch</h2>\n<p>Twitch <strong>VODs</strong> and <strong>clips</strong> download by pasting their link. For a subscriber-only VOD, first sign in to your\nTwitch account in the built-in browser (<strong>SNIFFER</strong>): Orbit reuses that session.</p>\n<h2 id=\"file-hosts\">File hosts</h2>\n<p>File host links (1fichier, MediaFire, Pixeldrain, Gofile…) also go in the bar. Orbit opens the page in the\nbackground, clicks the free download button, waits for the countdown if there is one, then downloads over\n<strong>several connections</strong> when the site allows it (often much faster than a browser). If a captcha shows up, the\nwindow appears so you can solve it.</p>\n<p>Limits set by a free site (waiting, capped speed) stay those of the site: Orbit does not bypass them.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-built-in-browser-sniffer\">The built-in browser (Sniffer)</h2>\n<p>Some pages hide their video (embedded players, sites that need a login). Click <strong>SNIFFER</strong>: a browser opens\ninside Orbit. Go to the page and play the video: Orbit detects the streams and offers to download them.\nStreams in pieces (HLS, DASH) are rebuilt into one file.</p>\n<h2 id=\"subscriptions\">Subscriptions</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Subscriptions</strong> tab follows channels or playlists and downloads new videos on its own.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Paste the address of a channel or a playlist (for example <code>youtube.com/@creator</code>).</li>\n<li>Pick <strong>Video</strong> or <strong>Audio (MP3)</strong>, then <strong>Subscribe</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure><a href=\"images/subscriptions.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Subscriptions tab\" src=\"images/subscriptions.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Subscriptions tab</figcaption></figure>\n<p>For each subscription, set the <strong>Quality</strong>, the <strong>Number of videos</strong> (the latest N or <strong>All</strong>) and <strong>No Shorts\nor lives</strong>. At the top, the check interval sets how often Orbit looks for new videos, and <strong>Check all</strong> checks\nright now. Each subscription can be paused, checked alone or removed.</p>\n<p>To keep your subscriptions when you change PC: <strong>Menu › Tools › Export/Backup Subscriptions</strong>, then\n<strong>Import/Restore Subscriptions</strong> on the other PC.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"interface.html\"><span>Previous</span>The interface</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"conversion.html\"><span>Next</span>Conversion</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#download-a-video\">Download a video</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#quality-and-format\">Quality and format</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-download-list\">The download list</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#music-spotify-apple-music-deezer-and-csv\">Music: Spotify, Apple Music, Deezer and CSV</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#twitch\">Twitch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#file-hosts\">File hosts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-built-in-browser-sniffer\">The built-in browser (Sniffer)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#subscriptions\">Subscriptions</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../telechargements.html"}, "conversion.html": {"title": "Conversion — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"conversion\">Conversion</h1>\n<h2 id=\"the-converter\">The Converter</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Converter</strong> turns almost any kind of file into another. Drop files or <strong>whole folders</strong> (Orbit goes\nthrough subfolders) in the area, or click the files or folder button. Orbit recognizes each file and offers the\npossible output formats.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/convertpro.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Converter, ready for files\" src=\"images/convertpro.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Converter, ready for files</figcaption></figure>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Input</th>\n<th>Output</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Video</td>\n<td>MP4, MKV, MOV, AVI, WEBM…</td>\n<td>MP4, MOV, ProRes, MKV, WEBM, AVI, GIF, or audio extraction (MP3, WAV, FLAC, M4A)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audio</td>\n<td>MP3, WAV, FLAC, M4A, OGG…</td>\n<td>WAV, MP3, FLAC, AAC, OGG, OPUS, M4A, with tag editing (title, artist, album, year, cover)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Image</td>\n<td>JPG, PNG, WEBP, HEIC, TIFF, BMP…</td>\n<td>PNG, JPG, WEBP, AVIF, TIFF, BMP</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>LUT</td>\n<td><code>.cube</code>, <code>.3dl</code></td>\n<td><code>.cube</code> ↔ <code>.3dl</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fonts</td>\n<td>TTF, OTF</td>\n<td>TTF, WOFF, WOFF2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3D</td>\n<td>FBX, OBJ, GLB, GLTF, STL, PLY, DAE…</td>\n<td>GLB, OBJ, STL, PLY</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Documents</td>\n<td>DOCX, XLSX, Markdown</td>\n<td>PDF, HTML</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>After Effects</td>\n<td><code>.ffx</code>, <code>.aep</code></td>\n<td>analysis (effects and required plugins) and After Effects version change</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"video-settings\">Video settings</h3>\n<p>Select a video file to see its settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Encoder</strong>: <strong>Auto (GPU if available)</strong>, <strong>NVIDIA GPU (NVENC)</strong> (much faster) or <strong>Processor (CPU)</strong> (slightly\n  smaller files). If the GPU fails, Orbit retries on the processor by itself.</li>\n<li><strong>Codec</strong>: H.264 (works everywhere), H.265, AV1, or <strong>fast copy</strong> (no re-encoding, instant, when the output\n  format allows it).</li>\n<li><strong>Quality</strong>: high, balanced or small, and a <strong>maximum height</strong> (1080p, 720p…).</li>\n<li><strong>Target size</strong>: to stay under an upload limit: <strong>Discord (10 MB)</strong>, <strong>WhatsApp (16 MB)</strong>, <strong>E-mail (25 MB)</strong>,\n  <strong>Discord Nitro (50 MB)</strong>, <strong>Nitro+ (500 MB)</strong> or a custom size.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Every audio track and the subtitles are kept when the container accepts them. If a track cannot be kept (for\nexample image subtitles in an MP4), the row says so in orange.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-queue\">The queue</h3>\n<p>Drag a row by its handle to change the order: the queue always takes the first waiting row, even if you\nreorder it during the conversion. With the graphics card, two videos are converted at the same time.</p>\n<h3 id=\"after-effects\">After Effects</h3>\n<p>For a <code>.ffx</code> preset or a <code>.aep</code> project, Orbit lists the effects used and the <strong>third-party plugins required</strong>.\nIt can also change the After Effects version of a file so it opens in an older or newer version, and, if After\nEffects is installed on your PC, use it to save a project in another version or apply a preset to a\ncomposition.</p>\n<h2 id=\"handbrake\">HandBrake</h2>\n<p>The <strong>HandBrake</strong> tab drives the well-known encoder for advanced compression. The first time, click <strong>Install\nHandBrake</strong> (automatic download).</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/handbrake.jpg\"><img alt=\"The HandBrake tab\" src=\"images/handbrake.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The HandBrake tab</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop your videos in the area (several at once).</li>\n<li>Select a file to set its encoding, or set it once and apply it to the whole queue.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Encode queue</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The settings, by section:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preset &amp; Format</strong>: an official HandBrake preset as a base, or <strong>None (manual settings)</strong>; container; <strong>Web\n  optimized (progressive playback)</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Video</strong>: encoder, encoding speed, <strong>Constant quality (RF)</strong> (lower = better) or <strong>Average bitrate</strong> with\n  <strong>2-pass</strong>; maximum resolution; frames per second; rotation. The estimated size is shown.</li>\n<li><strong>Filters</strong>: denoise (NLMeans), sharpen (Lapsharp), deinterlace, deblock, black and white.</li>\n<li><strong>Audio &amp; Output</strong>: <strong>Copy (no re-encoding)</strong> or audio bitrate; <strong>Keep subtitles</strong>; output folder.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Save your settings as a personal preset to find them later.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"telechargements.html\"><span>Previous</span>Downloads</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"ia-image.html\"><span>Next</span>AI for images</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#the-converter\">The Converter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#handbrake\">HandBrake</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../conversion.html"}, "ia-image.html": {"title": "AI for images — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"ai-for-images\">AI for images</h1>\n<p>These four tools are part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>. They run on your computer; the models download the\nfirst time you need them.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-generation\">AI Generation</h2>\n<p>Describe an image, Orbit creates it.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/imagegen.jpg\"><img alt=\"AI Generation: the description on the left, your creations on the right\" src=\"images/imagegen.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>AI Generation: the description on the left, your creations on the right</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Write the <strong>Description (prompt)</strong>: what you want to see, the style, the light. <strong>Auto prompt enhancement</strong>\n   fills out a short description.</li>\n<li>Pick a <strong>Style</strong>: None, Photorealistic, Cinematic, 3D / Blender, Anime, Digital Art, Watercolor, Cyberpunk,\n   Minimalist, Logo / Vector.</li>\n<li>Pick the <strong>AI model</strong>:<ul>\n<li><strong>Orbit Local — FLUX Klein on your GPU</strong>: the best understanding of descriptions, can write legible text;\n needs an NVIDIA card and the engine installed by <a href=\"ia-video-3d.html#paint-a-plate\">Paint a plate</a>;</li>\n<li><strong>Orbit Local — SDXL on your GPU</strong>: NVIDIA card, about 7 GB to download the first time;</li>\n<li><strong>Flux</strong> (free online service): for PCs without an NVIDIA card; adds a watermark and limits the size, about\n one image every 45 seconds.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Set the <strong>Format / Ratio</strong> (1:1, 16:9, 9:16, 4:3, 3:4, 3:2, 21:9), the <strong>Number of images</strong> (1 to 4) and the\n   <strong>Seed</strong>: a fixed seed gives the same image again, handy to tune a description word by word.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Generate the image</strong> (or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd>). With the local engines, the image shows up\n   and sharpens live while it is computed.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Each image of the gallery has its buttons: open, open the folder, <strong>Reuse prompt + seed</strong>, copy the prompt, see\nthe logs, delete. Adding to the queue chains several descriptions.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-magic-eraser\">AI Magic Eraser</h2>\n<p>Erase an object from a photo, or replace it with something else, like Photoshop's generative fill.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/inpaint.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Magic Eraser: tools on the left, photo in the middle\" src=\"images/inpaint.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Magic Eraser: tools on the left, photo in the middle</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop a photo in the area (JPG, PNG, WEBP, TIFF, AVIF…).</li>\n<li>Select the area to change:<ul>\n<li><strong>AI selection (click the object)</strong>: click an object, its outline is found for you; click again to grow\n it, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+click or right-click to remove a part;</li>\n<li><strong>Detect objects</strong> offers every object found in the photo;</li>\n<li><strong>Brush</strong> and <strong>Eraser</strong> to paint or fix the area by hand.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>In the prompt field (optional):<ul>\n<li>leave it empty and click <strong>🧽 Erase</strong>: the object disappears, the background is rebuilt;</li>\n<li>describe what to put instead (\"a leather backpack\", \"a tree\") and click <strong>✨ Generate / Replace</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>The result is saved in the <strong>Output folder</strong>; <strong>Undo the last removal</strong> goes back.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The <strong>Engine</strong> is chosen above the tools:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FLUX Klein</strong>: understands the whole scene, works on the full image up to 1920 pixels; NVIDIA card and the\n  <a href=\"ia-video-3d.html#paint-a-plate\">Paint a plate</a> engine. Used to replace (erasing always goes through LaMa, which\n  is more reliable);</li>\n<li><strong>Standard</strong>: LaMa to erase, Stable Diffusion to generate, with three levels: <strong>Fast</strong> (modest PC),\n  <strong>Quality</strong> (powerful PC) and <strong>SDXL HQ</strong> (NVIDIA card, about 6.5 GB the first time).</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>To replace a background, select the <strong>background</strong>, not the person: only the selected area changes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"ai-cutout\">AI Cutout</h2>\n<p>Removes the background of a video, without a green screen.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/matting.jpg\"><img alt=\"AI Cutout\" src=\"images/matting.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>AI Cutout</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop one or more videos.</li>\n<li>Select a file and set:<ul>\n<li><strong>Model &amp; quality</strong>: <strong>Fast (512p)</strong>, <strong>Balanced (960p)</strong> or <strong>Max (source)</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Background</strong>: transparent (<strong>WebM VP9</strong>, <strong>ProRes 4444</strong> or <strong>PNG sequence</strong>, ready for After Effects and\n Premiere), a background color, a blur or a background image;</li>\n<li><strong>Edge refinement</strong>: soften the edges, shrink or grow the mask to remove a fringe.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Preview (3s)</strong> shows the result over 3 seconds (the checkerboard = transparent areas).</li>\n<li><strong>Cut out</strong>, or <strong>Apply to the whole queue</strong> then <strong>Run queue</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"ai-enhance\">AI Enhance</h2>\n<p>Upscales, cleans and stabilizes your videos and images.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/enhance.jpg\"><img alt=\"AI Enhance\" src=\"images/enhance.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>AI Enhance</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Three tabs: <strong>Queue &amp; Settings</strong>, <strong>Before/After Preview</strong> (compare a frame before you start) and <strong>GPU\nPerformance</strong> (live load and memory of the card).</p>\n<p>The settings, by section:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI Upscale (Real-ESRGAN)</strong>: model, scale or target resolution, tile size (smaller if the card has little\n  memory), <strong>TTA</strong> mode (best quality, slower);</li>\n<li><strong>Video restoration</strong>: denoise (classic and temporal), compression recovery, anti-banding, detail recovery,\n  deinterlace, brightness, contrast, saturation, gamma;</li>\n<li><strong>Stabilization</strong> in two passes, with smoothing, sensitivity and auto zoom to hide the edges;</li>\n<li><strong>Frame interpolation (RIFE)</strong>: output frames per second or slow motion;</li>\n<li><strong>Sharpening &amp; Export</strong>: artifact-free sharpening, format and codec.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Save your settings as a preset, then <strong>Run queue</strong>.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"conversion.html\"><span>Previous</span>Conversion</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"ia-video-3d.html\"><span>Next</span>AI for video and 3D</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#ai-generation\">AI Generation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-magic-eraser\">AI Magic Eraser</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-cutout\">AI Cutout</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-enhance\">AI Enhance</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../ia-image.html"}, "ia-video-3d.html": {"title": "AI for video and 3D — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"ai-for-video-and-3d\">AI for video and 3D</h1>\n<h2 id=\"ai-interpolator\">AI Interpolator</h2>\n<p>Makes a video smoother by inventing the missing frames: 30 fps becomes 60, 120 or 240 fps, or a perfect slow\nmotion. Part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/interpolator.jpg\"><img alt=\"The AI Interpolator\" src=\"images/interpolator.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The AI Interpolator</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Source video</strong>: <strong>Browse</strong> or drop a file.</li>\n<li><strong>Output folder</strong>: where to save the result.</li>\n<li><strong>Multiplier</strong>: ×2, ×4, ×8 or <strong>Custom</strong>; then the <strong>Format</strong> and the <strong>Codec</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>GPU</strong>: the card to use; <strong>After</strong>: what Orbit does at the end (nothing, open the folder…).</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Interpolate!</strong>; the <strong>Console</strong> follows each step (extraction, interpolation, rebuild).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The <strong>Presets</strong> tab offers ready settings: <strong>RIFE x2 - Anime-optimized</strong>, RIFE x2 lossless quality, <strong>RIFE x4 -\nSlow-mo x0.5</strong>, <strong>RIFE x4 - 120FPS</strong>, <strong>RIFE x2 → GIF</strong>, <strong>RIFE x8 - 240FPS</strong>. The RIFE engine works with every\nrecent graphics card (Vulkan) and downloads the first time.</p>\n<h2 id=\"topaz-video-ai\">Topaz Video AI</h2>\n<p>Drives <strong>your own</strong> Topaz Video AI install from Orbit, with a queue and a before/after preview. Topaz Video AI\nmust be installed and activated on your PC (Topaz licence). Part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/topaz.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Topaz Video AI tab\" src=\"images/topaz.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Topaz Video AI tab</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Orbit finds Topaz by itself (<strong>Engine detected</strong>); otherwise, <strong>Re-run detection</strong>. The settings follow Topaz's:\n<strong>Enhance &amp; Upscale</strong> (AI model, scale, compression reduction, detail, sharpness, noise, dehalo, grain), frame\ninterpolation (frames per second, slow motion), <strong>Stabilization</strong> (strength, shake, rolling shutter) and\n<strong>Export</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paint-a-plate\">Paint a plate</h2>\n<p>Retouch a video shot by painting its first frame: erase an object, add one, change the light or add smoke,\nfire, steam. The AI applies the retouch to the whole shot.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/paintaplate.jpg\"><img alt=\"Paint a plate: tools on the left, frame in the middle, history on the right\" src=\"images/paintaplate.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Paint a plate: tools on the left, frame in the middle, history on the right</figcaption></figure>\n<h3 id=\"install\">Install</h3>\n<p>Paint a plate relies on <strong>ComfyUI</strong> and on the open-source <strong>Paint a plate</strong> pack (AInVFX). The tab guides the\ninstall:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>ComfyUI folder</strong>: pick an existing ComfyUI, or <strong>Install ComfyUI</strong> (official portable version, about 2 GB).</li>\n<li><strong>Hugging Face token</strong> (<code>hf_…</code>): some models need one. <strong>Create a token</strong> opens the Hugging Face page; then\n   paste it in the field. It stays on your PC.</li>\n<li><strong>Install what is missing</strong>: the main models (about 61 GB), in the ComfyUI folder. The optional models add\n   <strong>fluid shots</strong> (0.65 GB) and <strong>SDR to HDR</strong> (1.3 GB, licence to accept on Hugging Face).</li>\n<li><strong>Start Paint a plate</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You need an <strong>NVIDIA</strong> card with 16 GB of video memory for comfortable use. The ComfyUI launch options can limit\nthe memory used (for example <code>--reserve-vram 4 --cache-ram 16</code> on a 16 GB card). The <strong>Stop</strong> button shuts\nComfyUI down and frees the video memory.</p>\n<h3 id=\"retouch-a-shot\">Retouch a shot</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Open a shot: pick the video. Its format, frame rate and frame count show at the top.</li>\n<li>Pick the tool: <strong>Paint</strong> (add or replace), <strong>Erase</strong> (with <strong>Whole object</strong> to select the whole object in one\n   click) or <strong>Light</strong> (relight).</li>\n<li>Paint on the frame, then write the <strong>Description</strong> of the retouch and click <strong>Generate</strong>.</li>\n<li>Compare with <strong>Compare</strong>, play the shot with the bottom bar, then <strong>Export</strong>: the video keeps the source\n   format (codec, frame rate, timecode).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For a <strong>fluid shot</strong> (smoke, steam, fire), paint flat color areas on frame 0 and on the last frame, describe the\nfluid, then <strong>Generate</strong>. The <strong>history</strong>, on the right, keeps every try; <strong>Other seed</strong> runs a variant.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-3d-creation\">AI 3D Creation</h2>\n<p>Turns an image into a <strong>textured 3D model</strong>, right on your graphics card (TRELLIS.2 engine). Free tool.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/image3d.jpg\"><img alt=\"AI 3D Creation: settings on the left, 3D preview in the middle\" src=\"images/image3d.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>AI 3D Creation: settings on the left, 3D preview in the middle</figcaption></figure>\n<h3 id=\"install-1\">Install</h3>\n<p>You need an <strong>NVIDIA</strong> card. The first time, click <strong>Install the engine</strong>: Orbit installs Python, PyTorch and the\nlibraries, then the models (several GB). You can keep using Orbit during the install; if it is interrupted, it\nresumes where it stopped.</p>\n<h3 id=\"create-a-model\">Create a model</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop an <strong>Image</strong>: one object, clearly visible, on a simple background gives the best results. No image?\n   Describe the object (\"a wooden barrel\") and click <strong>Create the image</strong> (SDXL, locally).</li>\n<li><strong>Extra references</strong> (experimental): other photos of the same object from other angles.</li>\n<li>Set the <strong>Quality</strong> (<strong>Fast</strong>, <strong>High</strong>, <strong>Ultra</strong>) and the number of <strong>Faces</strong>. With less than 20 GB of\n   video memory, the resolution is lowered automatically when needed.</li>\n<li>Options: <strong>Generate the texture</strong> (off = geometry only, much faster), <strong>Remove background</strong>, <strong>Clean remesh</strong>,\n   texture size, steps, seed.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create the 3D model</strong>. Count one to three minutes depending on the quality.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"view-improve-export\">View, improve, export</h3>\n<p>The preview turns the model around, with several views: <strong>Texture</strong>, <strong>Clay</strong>, <strong>Mesh</strong>, <strong>Normals</strong>, <strong>UV</strong>.\nThen:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Enhance texture</strong>: adds detail with FLUX.2 klein without changing the colors or the shape (15 GB to download\n  the first time; intensity <strong>Light</strong>, <strong>Medium</strong>, <strong>Strong</strong>);</li>\n<li><strong>Optimize polygons + UVs</strong>: a much lighter mesh that keeps the look;</li>\n<li><strong>Rig</strong>: adds a skeleton with <strong>Rigify</strong> (automatic) or your own <strong>Auto-Rig Pro</strong> (Blender installed\n  required), then <strong>Open the rig in Blender</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Export</strong>: GLB, OBJ, STL, PLY, or <strong>Rigged FBX</strong> (skeleton, weights and textures for Unity or Unreal).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All your creations stay in the gallery at the bottom of the screen.</p>\n<h2 id=\"pbr-materials\">PBR Materials</h2>\n<p>Turns <strong>a single photo</strong> of a surface (wood, stone, concrete, fabric…) into a <strong>complete PBR material</strong>, ready\nfor Blender, Unreal, Unity or Substance. Part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>; NVIDIA card required.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Install PBR Materials</strong> (once).</li>\n<li><strong>Surface photo</strong>: drop a photo taken <strong>straight on</strong>, without perspective.</li>\n<li><strong>Create the material</strong>: the AI analyses the surface (a few seconds) and the <strong>Live preview</strong> shows the\n   material on a lit 3D plane.</li>\n<li>Adjust if needed:<ul>\n<li><strong>Resolution</strong> (up to 4K) and <strong>Seamless</strong> (the texture repeats with no visible seam);</li>\n<li><strong>Flatten the photo's lighting</strong>: removes shadows from the colour;</li>\n<li><strong>Relief</strong>: <strong>Normal strength</strong>, fine details or large shapes, height contrast, relief direction\n (light = up or dark = up, <strong>Auto</strong> by default);</li>\n<li><strong>Occlusion</strong>, <strong>Roughness</strong> (level, variation) and <strong>Metal</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Export</strong>: colour (albedo), OpenGL <strong>and</strong> DirectX normals, height, roughness, metal, occlusion, plus an\n   optional <strong>.glb</strong> file to preview in Blender, Unity or on the web.</li>\n</ol>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The best results come from a sharp photo, taken in overcast weather (soft light), straight on.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"ai-mocap\">AI Mocap</h2>\n<p>Turns a <strong>video</strong> into a <strong>3D animation</strong>: the filmed person's movement becomes an animated skeleton, with no\nsuit or sensors. Part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>; NVIDIA card required.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Install AI mocap</strong> (once).</li>\n<li><strong>Video</strong>: paste a link or drop a file. Best result: the whole body in frame, no cuts. Choose the start and\n   the duration; videos longer than one minute are captured in one-minute takes.</li>\n<li><strong>People</strong>: the one most present in the video, or another one.</li>\n<li><strong>Camera</strong>: <strong>Auto</strong> (Orbit detects whether the camera moves), <strong>Fixed</strong> (camera on a tripod, the most\n   stable) or <strong>Moving</strong> (pan, tracking shot, handheld: the camera movement is removed).</li>\n<li><strong>Motion quality</strong>: <strong>Ground contacts</strong> (flat floor, stairs or free), foot locking, hands on support\n   (push-ups, walls), <strong>Smoothing</strong> (from none to strong).</li>\n<li><strong>Face (ARKit expressions)</strong> option: also records facial expressions (Live Link Face CSV).</li>\n<li><strong>Capture motion</strong>. The <strong>Live preview</strong> shows the detected body points during the computation.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Export as</strong> BVH, FBX, GLB or .blend. FBX, GLB and .blend need <a href=\"https://www.blender.org\">Blender</a> (free):\nwithout it, only the BVH is created. Ready-made profiles for Blender, Unreal Engine and Mixamo.</p>\n<h3 id=\"apply-it-to-your-character\">Apply it to your character</h3>\n<p>In <strong>Character</strong>, pick your model (FBX, GLB, VRM or .blend): Orbit recognises its bones on its own (Mixamo,\nUnreal, Unity, Rigify, VRoid…). <strong>Adjust bones</strong> lets you fix a match. Tick <strong>In place (no travel)</strong> for an\nanimation that does not move around, then <strong>Apply to my character</strong> and <strong>Open in Blender</strong>.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"ia-image.html\"><span>Previous</span>AI for images</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"voix-musique-ia.html\"><span>Next</span>Voice, dubbing and music AI</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#ai-interpolator\">AI Interpolator</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#topaz-video-ai\">Topaz Video AI</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#paint-a-plate\">Paint a plate</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-3d-creation\">AI 3D Creation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#pbr-materials\">PBR Materials</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-mocap\">AI Mocap</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../ia-video-3d.html"}, "voix-musique-ia.html": {"title": "Voice, dubbing and music AI — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"voice-dubbing-and-music-ai\">Voice, dubbing and music AI</h1>\n<p>Five tools to create sound with AI, <strong>on your own PC</strong>: voice-overs, dubbing a video into another language,\nsound effects, music, and a live voice changer. They are all part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a> and need an\n<strong>NVIDIA</strong> graphics card (except Kokoro and the voice changer, which also run on the processor).</p>\n<p>Nothing is sent online: no subscription, no character limit, no watermark.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-voice\">AI Voice</h2>\n<p>A voice-over studio: write a text, pick a voice, Orbit reads it.</p>\n<h3 id=\"install-an-engine\">Install an engine</h3>\n<p>On first launch, <strong>Choose an engine</strong> opens the list of <strong>Voice engines</strong>:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Engine</th>\n<th>Strengths</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Kokoro</strong></td>\n<td>Ultra fast and light, works without a graphics card. Ready-made voices (only one French voice).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Qwen3-TTS</strong></td>\n<td>Creates a voice from a description and clones a clip. Very natural in French.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>VoxCPM2</strong></td>\n<td>The most faithful cloning, 30 languages, 48 kHz audio. Also creates voices from a description.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The first install also adds PyTorch (about 3 GB), shared by the three engines.</p>\n<h3 id=\"generate-a-voice\">Generate a voice</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Pick a voice in <strong>My voices</strong> (<strong>Ready</strong>, <strong>Created</strong> or <strong>Cloned</strong> voices).</li>\n<li>Write the text. Set the <strong>Text language</strong>, the <strong>Speed</strong> and, with VoxCPM2, the <strong>Tone / emotion</strong> (for\n   example \"enthusiastic, smiling\").</li>\n<li><strong>Generate voice</strong> (or <code>Ctrl+Enter</code>). Long texts are read sentence by sentence with the same voice.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Each render goes to the history: <strong>Listen</strong>, <strong>Export as MP3</strong>, <strong>Open folder (WAV)</strong> or <strong>Reuse text,\nvoice and seed</strong>. Files are saved in <code>Downloads\\Orbit\\Voix IA</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"create-a-voice-from-words\">Create a voice from words</h3>\n<p><strong>Design a voice</strong>: describe the voice (gender, age, timbre, accent…), write a <strong>Test sentence</strong>, then choose\n<strong>1 take</strong> or <strong>3 takes</strong>. Listen, keep your favourite take and give it a <strong>Name</strong>. The kept voice will always\nsound the same.</p>\n<h3 id=\"clone-a-voice\">Clone a voice</h3>\n<p><strong>Clone a voice</strong>: drop an audio or video clip, then choose the <strong>Part to clone</strong> (5 to 30 seconds of a single\nvoice) on the waveform. <strong>Use this part</strong> removes music, sound effects and background noise, then transcribes\nwhat is said. Compare <strong>Cleaned voice</strong> and <strong>Original</strong>, fix the transcript if needed, then <strong>Save voice</strong>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Only clone your own voice or the voice of someone who gave you their consent.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"ai-dubbing\">AI Dubbing</h2>\n<p>Dubs any video into another language, <strong>with each person's real voice</strong>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Video to dub</strong>: paste a link (YouTube, TikTok…) or <strong>Choose a file</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Dub into</strong>: one or more languages. Several languages = one audio track per language in the same video.</li>\n<li><strong>Voice acting</strong>: <strong>Steady</strong> (one steady voice per person, closest to the timbre) or <strong>Emotion of each\n   line</strong> (each line keeps the tone of the original: shouting, whispering…).</li>\n<li><strong>Translation</strong>: local Qwen3-14B (free, offline) or Claude with your API key. You can add <strong>Translation\n   instructions</strong> (informal \"you\", keep brand names…).</li>\n<li>Options: <strong>Keep the original track</strong>, <strong>Add subtitles</strong>. Then <strong>Dub the video</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Orbit downloads the video, separates voices from music, transcribes, recognises who speaks, translates, clones\neach voice, fits each line to the timing and remixes everything.</p>\n<p>The project then opens in the editor:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Lines</strong>: fix a text, <strong>Listen to the original</strong>, <strong>Listen to the dub</strong>, <strong>Another take (same text)</strong> or\n  <strong>Regenerate this line</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Voices</strong>: rename each speaker or replace <strong>Their real voice</strong> with a voice from the AI Voice tab;</li>\n<li><strong>Export with changes</strong> only redoes what changed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>An interrupted dub can be <strong>resumed</strong> where it stopped. Finished videos are in <code>Downloads\\Orbit\\Doublage IA</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-foley\">AI Foley</h2>\n<p>Gives sound to any video, even a silent one: footsteps, doors, engines, wind, impacts…</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Video</strong>: paste a link or <strong>Choose a file</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Sound effect intensity</strong>: stronger = more sounds and less risk of added music.</li>\n<li><strong>Video sound</strong>: <strong>Replace</strong> the sound, or <strong>Add to the original sound</strong> (with the <strong>Original sound</strong> /\n   <strong>Sound effects</strong> balance).</li>\n<li><strong>Generate sound effects</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The AI watches the video section by section, describes what it is going to make you hear, then generates\nsounds synced to the picture. To fix a section, edit its description (in English preferably) and run again:\nonly the sounds are redone. <strong>Another version</strong> gives a variant. Result as MP4 + WAV in\n<code>Downloads\\Orbit\\Bruitages IA</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-music\">AI Music</h2>\n<p>Composes full songs, with or without vocals, from an idea. ACE-Step 1.5 engine (MIT licence: <strong>your songs belong\nto you</strong>).</p>\n<p>Three modes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Simple</strong>: describe your idea (\"a happy pop song about holidays, male voice, in English\"), then <strong>Create the\n  music</strong>. The AI writes the style and lyrics for you.</li>\n<li><strong>Custom</strong>: write the <strong>Style</strong> and <strong>Lyrics</strong> yourself (or <strong>Write lyrics with AI</strong>), choose\n  <strong>Instrumental</strong> or <strong>With vocals</strong>, the <strong>Duration</strong>, <strong>Language</strong>, <strong>Tempo (BPM)</strong>, <strong>Key</strong> and number of\n  <strong>Variants</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Remix</strong>: drop a starting song, describe the <strong>New style</strong> and set the <strong>Faithfulness to the track</strong> (low =\n  very free style, high = keeps the melody and structure).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A one-minute song is composed in under a minute on a recent RTX card. In the history: <strong>Export as MP3</strong>,\n<strong>Remix this track</strong>, <strong>Reuse the settings</strong> or <strong>Redo a section</strong> (only that section is recomposed, the rest\ndoes not move).</p>\n<h2 id=\"voice-changer\">Voice Changer</h2>\n<p>Speak with another voice <strong>in real time</strong>, in Discord, OBS or a game.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Install the Voice Changer</strong> (without an NVIDIA card, it runs on the processor).</li>\n<li>Pick a <strong>Voice</strong>: a voice from the AI Voice tab, or <strong>Clone a voice</strong> from a 5 to 20 second clip of clear\n   speech.</li>\n<li>Choose the <strong>Mic</strong> and the <strong>Output</strong>. For Discord or OBS, install a virtual audio cable (VB-CABLE for\n   example) and choose it as the output: then select it as the microphone in Discord.</li>\n<li><strong>Start</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Useful settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Latency</strong>: <strong>Responsive</strong> (about 0.4 s delay, to talk in a game or a call) or <strong>Stable</strong> (about 0.65 s,\n  three times less computing, for a modest or very busy PC);</li>\n<li><strong>Height</strong> (the pitch, in semitones), <strong>Noise threshold (gate)</strong>, <strong>Output volume</strong>, <strong>Headphone monitoring</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Effect on/off shortcut</strong>: works even when Orbit is in the background (in game).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Convert a recording</strong> applies the voice to an audio or video file instead of the microphone (stop the live\nmode first).</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"ia-video-3d.html\"><span>Previous</span>AI for video and 3D</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"audio-transcription.html\"><span>Next</span>Audio and transcription</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#ai-voice\">AI Voice</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-dubbing\">AI Dubbing</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-foley\">AI Foley</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-music\">AI Music</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#voice-changer\">Voice Changer</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../voix-musique-ia.html"}, "audio-transcription.html": {"title": "Audio and transcription — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"audio-and-transcription\">Audio and transcription</h1>\n<h2 id=\"audio-studio\">Audio Studio</h2>\n<p>Processes the audio of a sound file <strong>or of a video</strong>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/audiostudio.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Audio Studio\" src=\"images/audiostudio.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Audio Studio</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop your audio files or videos in the area (several at once).</li>\n<li>Select a file and pick the <strong>Processing</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Processing</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Stem separation</strong></td>\n<td>splits vocals from music: <strong>2 stems</strong> (vocals + accompaniment), <strong>4 stems</strong> (vocals, drums, bass, other) or, with Demucs, <strong>6 stems</strong> (+ guitar and piano). <a href=\"premium.html\">Premium</a>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Denoise</strong></td>\n<td>reduces hiss and constant background noise; set the strength.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normalize</strong></td>\n<td>brings the volume to the level of streaming platforms (-14 LUFS, peak -1.5 dBTP).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Extract audio</strong></td>\n<td>takes the sound track out of a video, without re-encoding the picture, as WAV, MP3 or FLAC.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>Apply to the whole queue</strong> if needed, then <strong>Run queue</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For separation, two engines:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>High quality</strong> (Demucs v4): much better; with an NVIDIA card, it uses the GPU. Install: Demucs + PyTorch GPU\n  (about 2.5 GB) or CPU (about 700 MB). Stems come out as 320 kb/s MP3. <strong>Fast</strong> (about 4 times faster) or <strong>Max\n  quality</strong> (fine-tuned model).</li>\n<li><strong>Fast &amp; light</strong> (Spleeter): fair quality, about 700 MB to install.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"transcription\">Transcription</h2>\n<p>Turns the speech of a video or audio file into text and subtitles, on your computer. Part of\n<a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/transcription.jpg\"><img alt=\"Transcription\" src=\"images/transcription.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Transcription</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Choose a video or audio</strong> (MP4, MKV, MOV, MP3, WAV…).</li>\n<li><strong>Language</strong>: <strong>Auto-detect</strong> or the spoken language.</li>\n<li><strong>AI model</strong>: from the fastest (<strong>Base</strong>, about 142 MB) to the most accurate (heavier and slower).</li>\n<li><strong>Export to</strong>: tick the formats you want. Orbit prepares the right file for each program: <strong>Premiere Pro</strong>,\n   <strong>After Effects</strong>, <strong>CapCut</strong>, <strong>DaVinci Resolve</strong>, <strong>Final Cut Pro</strong>, <strong>YouTube / Web</strong>, <strong>Styled\n   subtitles</strong>, <strong>Plain text</strong>, <strong>Data</strong> and <strong>Lyrics</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Burn subtitles into the video</strong> also creates an <code>.mp4</code> with burned-in subtitles (not editable); set the font\n   size and color.</li>\n<li><strong>Output folder</strong> (next to the source file by default), then transcribe and export.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>When it is done, <strong>Open</strong> shows the files created.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"voix-musique-ia.html\"><span>Previous</span>Voice, dubbing and music AI</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"boite-a-outils.html\"><span>Next</span>Toolbox and media library</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#audio-studio\">Audio Studio</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#transcription\">Transcription</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../audio-transcription.html"}, "boite-a-outils.html": {"title": "Toolbox and media library — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"toolbox-and-media-library\">Toolbox and media library</h1>\n<h2 id=\"toolbox\">Toolbox</h2>\n<p>More than 60 small tools for everyday jobs, each on a single page: pick a tool, drop the file, set two or three\noptions, done.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/toolbox.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Toolbox: search at the top, tools by category\" src=\"images/toolbox.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Toolbox: search at the top, tools by category</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The search bar at the top finds a tool when you type what you want to do (\"gif\", \"compress\", \"audio\"…).</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Tools</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Video</td>\n<td>Trim, Compress to a size, Crop (social), Rotate / Mirror, Change speed, Reverse, Boomerang, Split into parts, Video → GIF, GIF → MP4, Images → GIF, Watermark / logo, Text watermark, Merge videos, Quick editor, Timeline editor, Slideshow, Screen recorder, Contact sheet, Extract frames, Thumbnail (instant), Convert video, Fade in/out, Denoise / deinterlace, Highlights (auto), Loop video, Replace audio</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audio</td>\n<td>Extract audio, Normalize / Fade, Cut silences, Merge audio, Voice + music, Audio editor, AI voice studio, Pitch &amp; tempo, Normalize (LUFS), Volume (gain), Audio visualizer, Waveform (image)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Image</td>\n<td>Convert an image, Clean metadata, Rotate / Mirror (image), Crop, Border / frame, Adjustments &amp; filters, Color palette, Apply a LUT, Colorize (AI), YouTube thumbnail, Comparator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Text and documents</td>\n<td>PDF tools, Burn subtitles, Translate subtitles, QR Code, OCR (text from image)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Files</td>\n<td>Batch rename, Watched folder</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Two tools deserve a word more:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Compress to a size</strong> aims at an exact weight: <strong>Discord (10 MB)</strong>, <strong>E-mail (25 MB)</strong>, <strong>Discord Nitro\n  (50 MB)</strong>, <strong>Nitro+ (500 MB)</strong> or a custom size.</li>\n<li><strong>Watched folder</strong> processes every file that lands in a folder: videos to MP4 (H.264), videos compressed to a\n  target size, videos to MP3, or images to another format. Handy for a captures or exports folder.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"media-library\">Media Library</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Media Library</strong> gathers your videos in a library, with a built-in player.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/library.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Media Library\" src=\"images/library.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Media Library</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Add</strong> files, or <strong>Scan</strong> a whole folder (subfolders included).</li>\n<li>On the left: <strong>Whole library</strong>, <strong>Recently added</strong>, <strong>Favorites</strong>, <strong>Resume playback</strong> (started videos resume\n  where you stopped) and <strong>Series</strong> (sorted by season and episode).</li>\n<li>At the top: instant search, <strong>Resolution</strong> and <strong>Codec</strong> filters, sorting by date added, name, duration, size\n  or season/episode.</li>\n<li>Click a video to play it. The <strong>Information</strong> panel shows the codecs, size and duration.</li>\n<li><strong>Creative export</strong>: <strong>Prepare for</strong> a use (editing, social…) picks the right preset, then <strong>Convert</strong>.</li>\n</ul>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"audio-transcription.html\"><span>Previous</span>Audio and transcription</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"drive.html\"><span>Next</span>Orbit Drive</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#toolbox\">Toolbox</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#media-library\">Media Library</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../boite-a-outils.html"}, "drive.html": {"title": "Orbit Drive — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"orbit-drive\">Orbit Drive</h1>\n<p><strong>Orbit Drive</strong> is your online storage, <strong>end-to-end encrypted</strong> (AES-256): your files are encrypted on your PC\nbefore they leave, neither the Orbit server nor Discord can read them. It is also used to <strong>share</strong> files by\nlink, <strong>sync</strong> folders from your PC and <strong>work together</strong> on the same folder. Everything in your Drive is also on\n<a href=\"https://orbit-drive.com\">orbit-drive.com</a>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The encrypted pieces are stored on Discord (or Telegram). These services are not made for this and an account\ncan be deleted: <strong>always keep another copy of your important files.</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The tab has three modes, top right: <strong>Cloud (account)</strong>, <strong>Drop</strong> and <strong>Local</strong> (Local mode only shows up if you\nalready use it).</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/drive.jpg\"><img alt=\"Orbit Drive\" src=\"images/drive.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Orbit Drive</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"sign-in\">Sign in</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Create account</strong> (e-mail and password) or <strong>Sign in</strong>. You can also sign in in one click with <strong>Google</strong>\n   or <strong>Discord</strong>: sign-in opens in your browser then comes back to Orbit on its own.</li>\n<li>Choose an <strong>encryption passphrase</strong>. It protects your <strong>vault</strong> (your files' keys) and works on all your\n   devices.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Each time you open it, type the passphrase to <strong>Unlock</strong> the Drive; <strong>Lock</strong> closes it.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Forgot password?</strong> sends a code by e-mail. It changes the sign-in password, not the passphrase.</li>\n<li><strong>Forgot your passphrase?</strong> creates a new one. Your personal files, impossible to decrypt without the old one,\n  are deleted; folders shared with you come back on their own.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Nobody can recover your passphrase, not even Orbit. Write it down somewhere safe.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"organize-your-files\">Organize your files</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Upload files</strong>, <strong>Upload a folder</strong> (with its subfolders) or drop them straight into the window. <strong>New\n  folder</strong> and <strong>Refresh</strong> are in the same bar.</li>\n<li><strong>Search</strong> by name, or type <code>#tag</code> to find everything with a tag.</li>\n<li><strong>Sort and filter</strong>: by name, date, size or type, either way; show only folders, videos, images, audio,\n  documents or archives. <strong>Grid</strong> or <strong>List</strong> view.</li>\n<li>Photos, videos and 3D models have a <strong>thumbnail</strong>, folders show a peek of their content, and creative files show\n  their software's logo (Blender, After Effects, Photoshop…).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"the-menu-of-a-file-or-folder\">The menu of a file or folder</h3>\n<p>Right-click (or the <strong>Actions</strong> button) on an item:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Action</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Open</strong> / <strong>Play</strong></td>\n<td>Opens a folder, plays a video or sound, shows a photo or 3D model</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Download</strong></td>\n<td>Saves the file (or the whole folder) to your PC</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Share link</strong></td>\n<td>Creates a share link, see below</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Share with people…</strong></td>\n<td>Invites other Orbit accounts into a folder</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sync to this PC…</strong></td>\n<td>Keeps this folder identical to a folder on your PC</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Rename</strong>, <strong>Move to…</strong></td>\n<td>Changes the name or location</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Copy to…</strong>, <strong>Duplicate</strong></td>\n<td>Instant copy: nothing is re-uploaded, and deleting the original does not touch the copy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Tags…</strong>, <strong>Color</strong></td>\n<td>Adds colour tags or colours a folder to spot it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Properties</strong></td>\n<td>Type, exact size, content, location, date, tags, encryption</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Delete</strong></td>\n<td>Deletes the item (<code>Del</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Select</strong> several items to move, copy, tag or delete them at once.</p>\n<h3 id=\"view-without-downloading\">View without downloading</h3>\n<p><strong>Double-click</strong> a photo or a 3D model (GLB, FBX, OBJ, STL, PLY) to open it in the viewer, without saving\nanything on your PC: <code>←</code> <code>→</code> for the next file in the folder, <code>Esc</code> to close. For 3D models, textures are found\non their own in the model's folder. Videos play directly.</p>\n<h3 id=\"transfers\">Transfers</h3>\n<p>Each upload or download can be <strong>paused</strong> and resumed, next to the Cancel button. <strong>Stop all</strong>, at the top of the\nDrive, cancels every running transfer and pauses syncs.</p>\n<h2 id=\"share-a-link\">Share a link</h2>\n<p><strong>Share link</strong> on a file or folder creates a link in one second (nothing is re-uploaded). Give the share a\n<strong>title</strong>, then choose:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Who can open the link</strong>: <strong>Anyone with the link</strong> or <strong>Only me</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>What people can do</strong>: <strong>View and download</strong>, or <strong>View only</strong> (the person watches and plays videos but\n  cannot save the files);</li>\n<li>a <strong>Password</strong> (optional): it never leaves your PC, give it separately;</li>\n<li>the <strong>Expiry</strong>: <strong>1 day</strong>, <strong>7 days</strong>, <strong>30 days</strong> or <strong>Never</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then <strong>Create the link</strong>: it is copied, with a <strong>QR code</strong> to scan or save. A folder link <strong>follows the\nfolder</strong>: what you add, delete or rename in it shows up for people who already have the link.</p>\n<p>Links open in any browser on <a href=\"https://orbit-drive.com\">orbit-drive.com</a>, without installing Orbit; the preview\nshown in Discord or WhatsApp displays the file's name, size and type.</p>\n<h2 id=\"drop-share-without-an-account\">Drop: share without an account</h2>\n<p><strong>Drop</strong> is <strong>Quick share</strong>: send encrypted files to someone, even without an account.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Send</strong>: drop your files or folders, the upload starts right away and each file gets its own link. <strong>Copy\n  link</strong>, <strong>QR code</strong>, <strong>Open in browser</strong>, or <strong>Copy all links</strong>. Unlimited size, files kept 30 days.</li>\n<li><strong>Receive</strong>: paste an orbit-drive.com link or a share code. A protected link asks for its password.</li>\n<li><strong>My shares</strong>: all your links, with their expiry. <strong>Disable the link</strong> cuts a link you already sent (files\n  stay in your Drive).</li>\n<li><strong>Shared folders</strong>: folders opened with a code (<code>orbf1_…</code>); you can <strong>Download all</strong>, play them or <strong>Save to\n  my Drive</strong>. With an account, this list follows you to your other PCs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"sync-a-folder-from-your-pc\">Sync a folder from your PC</h2>\n<p>Like Google Drive: a folder on your PC stays <strong>identical</strong> to a folder in the Drive, both ways. What you add,\nedit or delete goes up on its own, and other people's changes arrive in one to two seconds.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>In Cloud mode, open <strong>Sync with this PC</strong> then <strong>Sync a folder</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Folder on your PC</strong>: <strong>Choose a folder…</strong></li>\n<li><strong>In the Drive</strong>: a new folder with the same name in <strong>My Drive</strong>, or the open folder.</li>\n<li><strong>Sync</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The panel shows the status (up to date, files in progress, paused), the <strong>Recent activity</strong>, and the <strong>Sync\nnow</strong>, <strong>Pause</strong> / <strong>Resume</strong> and <strong>Stop syncing</strong> buttons (files stay on your PC and in the Drive).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Nothing is overwritten</strong>: if two people edit the same file at the same time, both versions are kept\n  (\"… (conflict - name date)\").</li>\n<li>If many files disappear from your PC at once, Orbit asks for a <strong>confirmation</strong>: <strong>Delete from Drive</strong>, or\n  <strong>No, put them back on my PC</strong>.</li>\n<li>With a synced folder, Orbit starts with Windows in the background (icon near the clock), catches up on what\n  changed while it was closed, and uses very little memory. <strong>Quit</strong> asks for confirmation.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"folders-shared-with-others\">Folders shared with others</h2>\n<p>To work together on the same project (Blender, After Effects…):</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Right-click a folder › <strong>Share with people…</strong>, type the person's <strong>Orbit account e-mail</strong>.</li>\n<li>Tick <strong>Can edit</strong> (otherwise they are <strong>Read-only</strong>), then <strong>Invite</strong>.</li>\n<li>The person gets an e-mail. Access opens as soon as they open their Drive once (with their passphrase).\n   Otherwise, send them the link with <strong>Copy invitation link</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>They find the folder in <strong>Shared with me</strong> and can sync it on their PC. <strong>People with access…</strong> lists the\nmembers; <strong>Remove access</strong>, <strong>Stop sharing</strong> or <strong>Leave this folder</strong> at any time. Encryption stays end-to-end.</p>\n<h2 id=\"store-on-telegram-or-your-own-discord\">Store on Telegram or your own Discord</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Telegram</strong>: stores your new files (encrypted) in your Telegram account's <strong>Saved Messages</strong>. You need an\n  <code>api_id</code> and an <code>api_hash</code> (on my.telegram.org › API development tools), then your number and the code you\n  receive. The Telegram connection stays on your PC.</li>\n<li><strong>Local mode</strong>: the file list and the key stay on your PC, the pieces go to your own Discord channel through a\n  <strong>webhook</strong> (Channel settings › Integrations › Webhooks › New webhook › Copy webhook URL). Several webhooks, one\n  per line, make uploads faster.</li>\n</ul>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"boite-a-outils.html\"><span>Previous</span>Toolbox and media library</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"reglages.html\"><span>Next</span>Settings</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#sign-in\">Sign in</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#organize-your-files\">Organize your files</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#share-a-link\">Share a link</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#drop-share-without-an-account\">Drop: share without an account</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#sync-a-folder-from-your-pc\">Sync a folder from your PC</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#folders-shared-with-others\">Folders shared with others</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#store-on-telegram-or-your-own-discord\">Store on Telegram or your own Discord</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../drive.html"}, "reglages.html": {"title": "Settings — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"settings\">Settings</h1>\n<p>Open the settings with <strong>Settings</strong>, at the bottom of the sidebar (or <code>Ctrl + ,</code>). The <strong>Sections</strong> bar, on the\nleft, lists the 15 pages; each page groups its settings in cards.</p>\n<h2 id=\"account\">Account</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Profile</strong>: your picture and <strong>Username</strong>, the same in the app and on orbit-drive.com. <strong>Change picture</strong> or\n  take back the Google / Discord one.</li>\n<li><strong>Account information</strong>: status, e-mail, first use, last activity, <strong>Device ID</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Your activity</strong>: finished jobs, tools used, space saved. Computed on your PC, never sent.</li>\n<li><strong>Data management</strong>: <strong>Export my data</strong> and <strong>Import settings</strong> (to move to another PC).</li>\n<li><strong>Danger zone</strong>: <strong>Delete account</strong> erases your account and all its data (Drive, shares, picture, Premium). You\n  must confirm with your password.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"achievements\">Achievements</h2>\n<p>25 badges, from Common to Legendary, unlocked by using Orbit (finished jobs, days in a row, tools tried, space\nsaved…). Nothing is sent. <strong>Pin</strong> up to 5 achievements in the <strong>Profile showcase</strong>, at the top of the settings.</p>\n<h2 id=\"security\">Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Orbit Drive account</strong>: your address and the state of your <strong>Encrypted vault</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>License &amp; device</strong>: the state of your Premium license, tied to a single device.</li>\n<li><strong>Secure connections</strong>: <strong>Verify HTTPS certificates</strong> (keep it on; an alert shows up if it is off, with a\n  button to turn it back on).</li>\n<li><strong>Active sessions</strong>: each device signed in to your Drive or Telegram, <strong>Revoke</strong> to close one. <strong>Sign out of\n  all devices</strong> closes every session (site, other PCs, browsers) except this one.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"notifications\">Notifications</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Desktop notifications</strong>: a Windows alert when a download or a render finishes (<strong>Test</strong> to try it).</li>\n<li><strong>Interface sounds</strong>: small click sounds.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"appearance\">Appearance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Theme</strong>: Nova, Graphite, Noir, Blanc, Minuit, or <strong>System</strong> (follows Windows light/dark mode), and <strong>Accent\n  color</strong>.</li>\n<li>Interface <strong>Language</strong>: French, English, Spanish, German, Italian, Portuguese.</li>\n<li><strong>Liquid glass (Apple style)</strong>: real refraction on the edge of panels and cards. <strong>Subtle</strong>, <strong>Apple</strong>,\n  <strong>Intense</strong> or <strong>Custom</strong> presets, then fine settings (refraction, prism effect, blur, tint, highlights,\n  mouse-following highlight, drop shadow), with a live preview.</li>\n<li><strong>Wallpaper</strong>: an image behind the glass, with its blur and darkening; tool page blur, text shadow and brighter\n  text keep text readable.</li>\n<li><strong>Setup wizard</strong>: <strong>Relaunch</strong> to reorganize the tabs for your profile (editor, 3D, audio…).</li>\n<li><strong>Reset</strong> puts the glass, wallpaper and text back to default.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"privacy\">Privacy</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Error reports</strong>: <strong>Automatic</strong> (sent when Orbit crashes, without your files or your user name) or <strong>Manual\n  only</strong> (only the ones you send from About).</li>\n<li><strong>Data on this device</strong>: the <strong>Usage history</strong> used for your stats and achievements, never sent; <strong>Clear</strong> to\n  start over.</li>\n<li><strong>What Orbit does with your data</strong>: a summary of what stays on your PC and what leaves.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"connections\">Connections</h2>\n<p>Link your accounts: <strong>Orbit Drive</strong> (encrypted storage and sharing), <strong>Google</strong> and <strong>Discord</strong> (one-click sign-in,\nprofile picture reused), <strong>Discord (storage)</strong> for Local mode and <strong>Telegram</strong> to store the Drive on your\naccount. <strong>Connect</strong>, <strong>Manage</strong>, <strong>Link</strong> or <strong>Unlink</strong> each one.</p>\n<h2 id=\"premium\">Premium</h2>\n<p>The state of your license (<strong>Active</strong>, <strong>Lifetime</strong> plan, activation date). <strong>Already paid: sync</strong> recovers a\nPremium paid on your account; <strong>Remove from this device</strong> frees it. See <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"cookies\">Cookies</h2>\n<p><strong>Browser cookies</strong>: Orbit reuses your browser's sign-in for videos reserved to subscribers or signed-in\naccounts.</p>\n<h2 id=\"downloads\">Downloads</h2>\n<p><strong>Output</strong>: <strong>Download folder</strong>, <strong>Default video format</strong>, restricted (ASCII) file names.</p>\n<p><strong>Embedded content</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Force H.264 (editing-friendly)</strong>: H.264/AAC for After Effects and Premiere, instead of VP9 or AV1;</li>\n<li><strong>Compress after download</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Audio only</strong>: keep only the sound (MP3, FLAC…);</li>\n<li>embed the thumbnail (cover), metadata (title, author, date), subtitles, chapters;</li>\n<li>auto-generated subtitles and subtitle languages (comma-separated codes, for example <code>fr.*,en.*</code>);</li>\n<li>write the .info.json;</li>\n<li>mark sponsor segments (SponsorBlock chapters) or remove sponsors (cuts intro, ads…).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Behavior</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Download archive</strong>: never download again what was already downloaded;</li>\n<li><strong>Ignore errors</strong>: keep going through a playlist if a video fails;</li>\n<li>keep the original timestamp, no .part files;</li>\n<li><strong>Concurrent fragments</strong>: speeds up HLS and DASH streams;</li>\n<li><strong>Speed limit</strong>: for example <code>5M</code> or <code>800k</code> (empty = unlimited);</li>\n<li><strong>Windows right-click menu</strong>: adds \"Orbit ▸ Compress / Crop…\" to the right-click menu of a file.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"ai--performance\">AI &amp; Performance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI Assistant</strong>: <strong>Free local AI</strong> (about 2 GB, downloaded once, works offline) or your <strong>Anthropic API key\n  (Claude)</strong>, more powerful. The key stays on your PC.</li>\n<li><strong>AI Enhance &amp; Topaz</strong>: <strong>Default AI output folder</strong> and <strong>Default GPU</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Simultaneous AI jobs (GPU)</strong>: how many AI tools use the graphics card at the same time. <strong>1</strong> (queue) is\n  recommended.</li>\n<li><strong>Maximum VRAM for AI</strong>: a video memory cap for AI engines, or <strong>Unlimited</strong>. Useful to keep room for a game or\n  another program. When Orbit goes to the background, idle engines give their video memory back after 30\n  seconds.</li>\n<li><strong>Performance</strong>:<ul>\n<li><strong>Visual effects</strong>: <strong>Auto</strong>, <strong>Full</strong> or <strong>Reduced</strong> (animated background, liquid glass, 3D intro). In Auto,\nOrbit lightens the effects on its own on a modest PC;</li>\n<li><strong>Disable hardware acceleration</strong> if the interface flickers (restart required);</li>\n<li>Converter <strong>Video encoding</strong>: Auto (GPU if available), NVIDIA GPU (NVENC) or Processor (CPU);</li>\n<li><strong>Max simultaneous downloads</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"modules\">Modules</h2>\n<p>The list of every installed engine and AI model (yt-dlp, ffmpeg, local AI, Real-ESRGAN, RIFE, HandBrake, Magic\nEraser, AI Voice, Mocap…), with their size and drive. Install, update, <strong>move to another drive</strong> or delete each\none to free space; a module other modules depend on is flagged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"network\">Network</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Proxy server</strong> and <strong>Test the proxy</strong> (checks the connection through yt-dlp).</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced</strong>: <strong>Custom yt-dlp arguments</strong>, added to every download.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"system\">System</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Startup &amp; window</strong>: <strong>Launch Orbit at Windows startup</strong>, <strong>Minimize to the notification area</strong> instead of\n  closing, <strong>Show Orbit in my Discord status</strong> (open tab and running downloads).</li>\n<li><strong>Storage</strong>: <strong>Temporary files</strong> (<strong>Clear</strong> button), <strong>AI modules location</strong> (choose the drive where modules\n  install; Orbit asks before each install) and <strong>Orbit data folder</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance</strong>: <strong>Re-install yt-dlp</strong> if downloads fail; <strong>JS engine for YouTube (Deno)</strong>, which avoids the\n  \"no supported JavaScript runtime\" error; <strong>View logs</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"about\">About</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Version</strong> and <strong>Check for updates</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Report a bug</strong>: describe the problem and click <strong>Send report</strong>.</li>\n</ul>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"drive.html\"><span>Previous</span>Orbit Drive</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"premium.html\"><span>Next</span>Orbit Premium</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#account\">Account</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#achievements\">Achievements</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#security\">Security</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#notifications\">Notifications</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#appearance\">Appearance</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#privacy\">Privacy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#connections\">Connections</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#premium\">Premium</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#cookies\">Cookies</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#downloads\">Downloads</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai--performance\">AI &amp; Performance</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#modules\">Modules</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#network\">Network</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#system\">System</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#about\">About</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../reglages.html"}, "premium.html": {"title": "Orbit Premium — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"orbit-premium\">Orbit Premium</h1>\n<p>Orbit is free. <strong>Orbit Premium</strong> unlocks the most advanced AI tools, for a <strong>one-time payment of €14.99</strong>, valid\n<strong>for life</strong> on <strong>1 device</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-is-included\">What is included</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Free</th>\n<th>Premium</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Downloads, Spotify, Twitch, file hosts, Subscriptions</td>\n<td>AI Generation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Converter and HandBrake</td>\n<td>AI Magic Eraser</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Toolbox and Media Library</td>\n<td>AI Cutout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audio Studio: denoise, normalize, extract</td>\n<td>AI Enhance</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AI 3D Creation</td>\n<td>AI Interpolator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Paint a plate</td>\n<td>Topaz Video AI</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Orbit Drive</td>\n<td>Transcription</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AI Assistant</td>\n<td>Audio Studio: stem separation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>AI Voice, AI Dubbing, AI Foley</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>AI Music, Voice Changer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>PBR Materials, AI Mocap</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>A Premium tool stays visible: when opened, it shows a locked screen with the button to go Premium.</p>\n<h2 id=\"buy\">Buy</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>Premium</strong> at the bottom of the sidebar (or <strong>Menu › File › Go Premium</strong>).</li>\n<li>Create an account or sign in to your Orbit account.</li>\n<li>Click the buy button (€14.99): payment opens in your browser (Stripe; card, or PayPal depending on your\n   country).</li>\n<li>Come back to Orbit: Premium unlocks by itself as soon as the payment is confirmed.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure><a href=\"images/premium.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Orbit Premium window\" src=\"images/premium.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Orbit Premium window</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Paid another way (crypto) or received a key? Use the \"Paid in crypto or received a key?\" link, then activate\nyour key.</p>\n<h2 id=\"gift-premium\">Gift Premium</h2>\n<p>To receive Premium as a gift, with no account or payment: open the Premium window, copy <strong>your device ID</strong> and\ngive it to the person offering it. Once confirmed, click the gift check button: Orbit activates.</p>\n<h2 id=\"good-to-know\">Good to know</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Premium tools run on your PC; once activated, Premium also works offline.</li>\n<li>Premium is tied to one device. To move to another PC, contact support.</li>\n<li>The button at the bottom of the sidebar reads <strong>Premium active</strong> when everything is unlocked.</li>\n</ul>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"reglages.html\"><span>Previous</span>Settings</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"depannage.html\"><span>Next</span>Troubleshooting</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#what-is-included\">What is included</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#buy\">Buy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#gift-premium\">Gift Premium</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#good-to-know\">Good to know</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../premium.html"}, "depannage.html": {"title": "Troubleshooting — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h1>\n<h2 id=\"a-download-fails\">A download fails</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>Failed — see logs</strong> on the row: the end of the log gives the reason.</li>\n<li>Sites change often: <strong>Settings › System › Re-install yt-dlp</strong> installs the latest version (Orbit also updates\n   it at every launch).</li>\n<li>For YouTube, if the log mentions \"JavaScript runtime\" or formats are missing: <strong>Settings › System</strong>, install\n   the JS engine for YouTube (Deno).</li>\n<li>Private, members-only or age-restricted content: turn on the <strong>Cookie</strong> icon of the bar (you must be signed in\n   to the site in Chrome), or open the page in the <strong>SNIFFER</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Menu › Downloads › Restart Failed Downloads</strong> restarts every failure.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"file-deleted-on-a-finished-download\">\"File deleted\" on a finished download</h2>\n<p>The file was moved or deleted from the disk. <strong>Download again</strong> gets it back, or remove the row.</p>\n<h2 id=\"orbit-closed-during-a-download\">Orbit closed during a download</h2>\n<p>Start Orbit again: downloads resume where they stopped. HandBrake and Topaz queues come back too, but you have\nto restart them by hand.</p>\n<h2 id=\"an-ai-tool-is-slow-or-runs-out-of-memory\">An AI tool is slow or runs out of memory</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Close games and programs that use the graphics card.</li>\n<li>Keep <strong>Settings › Downloads › Simultaneous AI jobs (GPU)</strong> at <strong>1</strong>.</li>\n<li>Set a <strong>Maximum VRAM for AI</strong> to leave some margin.</li>\n<li>In AI Enhance, lower the tile size; in AI 3D Creation, pick <strong>Fast</strong> or fewer <strong>Faces</strong>.</li>\n<li>In Paint a plate, use <strong>Stop</strong> when you are done: ComfyUI frees the video memory.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"an-nvidia-graphics-card-is-required\">\"An NVIDIA graphics card is required\"</h2>\n<p>AI 3D Creation, Paint a plate and local AI Generation use CUDA, which only exists on NVIDIA cards. On another PC,\nAI Generation goes through the online <strong>Flux</strong> service. The other AI tools (upscale, interpolation, cutout, magic\neraser) work with every recent card.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-interface-flickers-or-stays-black\">The interface flickers or stays black</h2>\n<p><strong>Settings › AI &amp; Performance › Disable hardware acceleration</strong>, then restart Orbit. If the interface is slow,\ntone down the <strong>Liquid glass</strong> (<strong>Subtle</strong> preset) or turn it off in <strong>Settings › Appearance</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"a-premium-tool-stays-locked\">A Premium tool stays locked</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Check the bottom of the sidebar: it should read <strong>Premium active</strong>.</li>\n<li>After a payment, open the Premium window: it unlocks as soon as the payment is confirmed.</li>\n<li><strong>Update required</strong>: your version is too old for the AI tools; click the button to install the latest one.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-antivirus-blocks-orbit-or-a-module\">The antivirus blocks Orbit or a module</h2>\n<p>Orbit downloads engines (yt-dlp, ffmpeg, AI models) into <code>C:\\Users\\&lt;you&gt;\\.orbit</code>. If your antivirus blocks one,\nadd this folder to its exceptions, then reinstall the module from <strong>Settings › Modules &amp; AI</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"free-up-space\">Free up space</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Settings › System › Temporary files › Clear</strong> deletes the work files.</li>\n<li><strong>Settings › Modules &amp; AI</strong>: remove the models of tools you do not use (they download again if needed).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"report-a-problem\">Report a problem</h2>\n<p><strong>Settings › About</strong>, bug report: describe what you were doing and what happened, then send the report. The last\n25 lines of the log are attached, without your user name. The full log is in <strong>Settings › System › View logs</strong>.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"premium.html\"><span>Previous</span>Orbit Premium</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#a-download-fails\">A download fails</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#file-deleted-on-a-finished-download\">\"File deleted\" on a finished download</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#orbit-closed-during-a-download\">Orbit closed during a download</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#an-ai-tool-is-slow-or-runs-out-of-memory\">An AI tool is slow or runs out of memory</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#an-nvidia-graphics-card-is-required\">\"An NVIDIA graphics card is required\"</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-interface-flickers-or-stays-black\">The interface flickers or stays black</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#a-premium-tool-stays-locked\">A Premium tool stays locked</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-antivirus-blocks-orbit-or-a-module\">The antivirus blocks Orbit or a module</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#free-up-space\">Free up space</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#report-a-problem\">Report a problem</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../depannage.html"}};
